FNV-1a is a non-cryptographic hash with no key. The default (`logQueries: false`) is a genuine privacy improvement over verbatim logging, but "non-reversible … without recording user content" overstates it: search queries are low-entropy natural language, so anyone holding a log line can confirm or recover a candidate query by hashing a dictionary (`hash("swift concurrency")` is a one-line offline check), and the 64-bit output is trivially attacked this way. Reachability: whoever reads the logs (a log collector, a pasted bug report, an operator) can recover queries that were never meant to be recorded. No code path is otherwise affected.

